From: Felipe Bonetto <felipesensbonetto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] XilinxPlatformCableUSB: skip set_interface_alt_setting on macOS

`libusb_set_interface_alt_setting(0, 1)` always fails with
`LIBUSB_ERROR_OTHER` on macOS for the XPCU cable. The driver already
logs a warning and continues, so JTAG operations on the same session
work. But the failure leaves the kernel-side USB endpoint in an
inconsistent state — after many program/restart cycles the control
endpoint stops responding entirely and `displayCableVersion()` times
out on the next session start. The cable is then unusable until a
physical unplug.

Skipping the call on Darwin avoids the bad state entirely. The cable
functions correctly on alt setting 0 (verified end-to-end: bitstream
programming, JTAG-UART scratch reads, IDCODE chain walk all worked
from alt 0 in earlier sessions before the cumulative state corruption
took the cable down).

--- a/src/xilinxPlatformCableUSB.cpp
+++ b/src/xilinxPlatformCableUSB.cpp
@@ -82,7 +82,15 @@
 		throw std::runtime_error("lowlevel init failed");
 	}

+#ifdef __APPLE__
+	/* macOS: libusb_set_interface_alt_setting(0, 1) always fails with
+	 * LIBUSB_ERROR_OTHER and leaves the control endpoint in an
+	 * inconsistent state after enough sessions. The cable works fine
+	 * on alt 0; skip the switch entirely. */
+	(void)0;
+#else
 	fx2->set_interface_alt_setting(0, 1);
+#endif

 	displayCableVersion();
